Parentheses around a pipeline that calls html or urlquery stay. html/template
allows those escapers only as the last command of a pipeline and does not look
inside a parenthesized one, so flattening it would make html/template reject
the template (PR #208 review). A parenthesized first command that calls
neither is still flattened.
-- input.gohtml --
<p>{{ (html .Name) | printf "%s" }}</p>
<a href="/q?{{ (urlquery .Name) | printf "q=%s" }}">x</a>
<p>{{ (printf "%s" .Name) | html }}</p>
<p>{{ (html .Name) }}</p>
-- format.gohtml --
<p>{{(html .Name) | printf "%s"}}</p>
<a href="/q?{{(urlquery .Name) | printf "q=%s"}}">x</a>
<p>{{printf "%s" .Name | html}}</p>
<p>{{(html .Name)}}</p>
-- data/empty.json --
{}
-- data/truthy.json --
{"Name":"a<b&c"}
